---
title: Owned compute, independent supervision, durable results
---
flowchart LR
  accTitle: PodVigil architecture
  accDescr: A local controller and detached watchdog share a job ledger. They manage an owned Runpod Secure Cloud Pod through the provider API. Inside the Pod a privileged guard supervises an unprivileged workload and snapshots local outputs to a private network volume. A local backup is verified before that volume can be deleted.

  subgraph LOCAL["YOUR COMPUTER"]
    direction TB
    CLI["podvigil command<br/>Plan, launch, inspect, recover"] --> CTRL["Controller<br/>Policy and ownership checks"]
    CTRL --> WATCH["Detached watchdog<br/>Independent deadline and recovery"]
    CTRL -.-> LEDGER[("Job ledger<br/>Ownership and cleanup evidence")]
    WATCH -.-> LEDGER
  end

  API["Runpod API<br/>Explicit Secure Cloud requests"]

  subgraph POD["OWNED SECURE CLOUD POD"]
    direction TB
    GUARD["Privileged guard and supervisor<br/>Deadline, snapshot and self-deletion"]
    WORK["Unprivileged workload<br/>No account or S3 credentials"]
    DISK[("Local Pod outputs")]
    GUARD --> WORK --> DISK
  end

  subgraph RESULTS["RESULT RECOVERY"]
    direction TB
    VOLUME[("Owned network volume<br/>Survives Pod termination")]
    VOLUME -->|"S3 retrieval after compute is gone"| BACKUP[("Verified local backup<br/>Artifacts and checksums")]
    BACKUP --> AUDIT["Audit all volume objects<br/>Then delete owned storage"]
  end

  LOCAL -->|"create, verify, delete"| API
  API --> POD
  POD -->|"supervisor snapshot"| RESULTS

  classDef primary fill:#eaf2ff,stroke:#3864a2,color:#142b49,stroke-width:2px;
  classDef store fill:#e7f5ef,stroke:#35745d,color:#163c2f,stroke-width:1.5px;
  classDef external fill:#f1ecfa,stroke:#7d60ad,color:#382650,stroke-width:2px;

  class CLI,CTRL,WATCH,GUARD,WORK,AUDIT primary;
  class LEDGER,BACKUP,DISK,VOLUME store;
  class API external;
